    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "1TH",
      "chapter": 5,
      "chapter_usfm": "1TH.5",
      "version_id": 100,
      "version_abbr": "NASB1995",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Now as to the times and the epochs, brethren, you have no need of anything to be written to you."
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For you yourselves know full well that the day of the Lord will come just like a thief in the night."
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "While they are saying, “Peace and safety!” then destruction will come upon them suddenly like labor pains upon a woman with child, and they will not escape."
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But you, brethren, are not in darkness, that the day would overtake you like a thief;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "for you are all sons of light and sons of day. We are not of night nor of darkness;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "so then let us not sleep as others do, but let us be alert and sober."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For those who sleep do their sleeping at night, and those who get drunk get drunk at night."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But since we are of the day, let us be sober, having put on the breastplate of faith and love, and as a helmet, the hope of salvation."
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For God has not destined us for wrath, but for obtaining salvation through our Lord Jesus Christ,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "who died for us, so that whether we are awake or asleep, we will live together with Him."
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Therefore encourage one another and build up one another, just as you also are doing."
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.12",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But we request of you, brethren, that you appreciate those who diligently labor among you, and have charge over you in the Lord and give you instruction,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and that you esteem them very highly in love because of their work. Live in peace with one another."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "We urge you, brethren, admonish the unruly, encourage the fainthearted, help the weak, be patient with everyone."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "See that no one repays another with evil for evil, but always seek after that which is good for one another and for all people."
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.16",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Rejoice always;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.17",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "pray without ceasing;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 18,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.18",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "in everything give thanks; for this is God’s will for you in Christ Jesus."
        },
        {
          "verse": 19,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.19",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Do not quench the Spirit;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 20,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.20",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "do not despise prophetic utterances."
        },
        {
          "verse": 21,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.21",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But examine everything carefully; hold fast to that which is good;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 22,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.22",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "abstain from every form of evil."
        },
        {
          "verse": 23,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.23",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Now may the God of peace Himself sanctify you entirely; and may your spirit and soul and body be preserved complete, without blame at the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ."
        },
        {
          "verse": 24,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.24",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Faithful is He who calls you, and He also will bring it to pass."
        },
        {
          "verse": 25,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.25",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Brethren, pray for us."
        },
        {
          "verse": 26,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.26",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Greet all the brethren with a holy kiss."
        },
        {
          "verse": 27,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.27",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I adjure you by the Lord to have this letter read to all the brethren."
        },
        {
          "verse": 28,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.28",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you."
        }
      ],
      "verse_count": 28,
      "headings": [
        {
          "before_verse": 12,
          "text": "Christian Conduct"
        }
      ],
